  "facts": [
    "Queensferry Crossing, a 1.7‑mile cable‑stayed marvel, opened on 30 August 2017, exactly fifty‑three years after Queen Elizabeth II inaugurated the older Forth Road Bridge, cementing a historic royal link.",
    "Designed to replace a 1964 bridge that was already exceeding its 11‑million‑vehicle‑per‑year capacity, Queensferry Crossing now handles 23 million vehicles annually, thanks to its three‑tower, 2.7‑kilometre span.",
    "Construction began in late 2011 after a £790 million bid by FCBC, and the bridge’s opening ceremony on 4 September 2017 marked the first time a Scottish bridge was formally named by public vote."
